    \"agent:main:subagent:3b89c0c7-c0b7-45d9-af18-aadb0b5fb280\",\n        \"agent:main:subagent:d9bc3cc5-63c0-4c06-aff4-85b041a007ad\"\n      ],\n      \"systemSent\": true,\n      \"abortedLastRun\": false,\n      \"lastChannel\": \"feishu\",\n      \"lastTo\": \"user:ou_fc1e75d64fec6e10ce94a51adc6f6409\",\n      \"lastAccountId\": \"default\",\n      \"transcriptPath\": \"/home/gem/workspace/agent/agents/main/sessions/629e0263-50d0-4f95-82e6-70c782a96a99.jsonl\",\n      \"messages\": [\n        {\n          \"role\": \"user\",\n          \"content\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"text\",\n              \"text\": \"System: [2026-04-09 11:57:20 GMT+8] Feishu[default] DM | ou_fc1e75d64fec6e10ce94a51adc6f6409 [msg:om_x100b52467736ece8c38be398d38b677]\\n\\n\\n\\nJSON.stringify({\\n  csrf: localStorage.getItem('lm_metadata') ? JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('lm_metadata')).csrf : 'not_found',\\n  session: localStorage.getItem('lm_metadata') ? JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('lm_metadata')).session : 'not_found'\\n})\\n'{\\\"csrf\\\":\\\"not_found\\\",\\\"session\\\":\\\"not_found\\\"}'\\nibrary/Application\\\\ Support/Google/Chrome/ 2>/dev/null | head -5\\nVM345:1 Uncaught SyntaxError: Invalid or unexpected token\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"timestamp\": 1775707043220,\n          \"__openclaw\": {\n            \"id\": \"29255f3a\",\n            \"seq\": 169\n          },\n          \"senderLabel\": \"ou_fc1e75d64fec6e10ce94a51adc6f6409\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"role\": \"assistant\",\n          \"content\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"thinking\",\n              \"thinking\": \"The console output is confusing - the error might be from the user trying to run a bash command in the browser console. Let me just focus on what we need.\\n\\nThe SID cookie was captured. But the CSRF/session tokens from localStorage returned 'not_found'. \\n\\nLet me try a different approach - look at the actual localStorage on the NotebookLM page. The tokens might be stored under different keys. Let me ask the user to run some JS to explore localStorage.\\n\\nAlso the error suggests the user might have pasted something incorrectly. Let me ask them to try just the JavaScript part in the console.\\n\\nActually, let me think about the simplest approach. The `storage_state.json` from Playwright contains all cookies from the browser session. \\n\\nIf we can get that file from the user's Mac, we don't need the tokens from localStorage since the `storage_state.json` should already have everything we need. The challenge is that Playwright's cookies are stored in a binary SQLite database, not as a simple JSON file, so we'd either need to export them through Playwright itself or find another way to access that data.\\n\\nLooking at what we've actually captured from the console - just a SID cookie - it's incomplete compared to what the Playwright storage state provides. I should ask the user to try running `playwright install chromium` with that command flag, or explore other paths to access the full cookie storage. We could also try reading the Chrome cookies database directly using a tool like `cookies.sql` if we can access the binary file through the filesystem, though that's getting quite involved.\\n\\nThe simplest path forward is probably just asking the user to try that install command again to see if it bypasses the Google CDN timeout issue.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"type\": \"text\",\n              \"text\": \"那个错误是你混在一起了，忽略它。\\n\\n关键问题：`playwright install chromium` 下载超时。让我换个思路——直接用国内可访问的工具来读取你的Chrome cookies。\\n\\n在你的Mac终端运行：\\n\\n```bash\\n# 检查Chrome的Cookies数据库路径\\nls ~/Library/Application\\\\ Support/Google/Chrome/Default/Cookies 2>/dev/null && echo \\\"Cookies found\\\"\\n```\\n\\n或者试试加速安装：\\n\\n```bash\\n# 用华为镜像加速\\nPLAYWRIGHT_DOWNLOAD_HOST=https://mirrors.huaweicloud.com/playwright python3 -m playwright install chromium\\n```\\n\\n或者干脆用你现有的 Chrome 路径直接指定：\\n\\n```bash\\